{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Analyzes modified source code files for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, best practices, readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "*.dart",
      "*.php",
      "*.js",
      "*.ts",
      "*.jsx",
      "*.tsx",
      "*.py",
      "*.java",
      "*.go",
      "*.rb",
      "*.cs"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code in this file for potential improvements. Check for:\n1. Code smells (duplicated code, long methods, large classes, too many parameters)\n2. Design pattern opportunities (could patterns like Factory, Strategy, Observer improve this?)\n3. Best practices violations (naming conventions, error handling, null safety)\n4. Readability issues (complex conditionals, nested loops, unclear variable names)\n5. Maintainability concerns (tight coupling, low cohesion, hard-coded values)\n6. Performance optimizations (unnecessary loops, inefficient queries, missing indexes)\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions while preserving existing functionality. Be concise and prioritize the most impactful improvements."
  }
}